# Personal AI Integration Plan – Administrative Assistant (HR & Engineering Coordination)

This plan outlines how AI will support three recurring tasks in my role.

---

## Task 1: Preparing HR Coordination Summaries
### Expected Benefit
Faster preparation of summaries with fewer manual errors.

### Preferred Prompt / Workflow
Use a structured C.A.R.E prompt to summarize HR requests without including personal data.

### Risk / Verification Requirement
Risk: Incorrect or incomplete HR details.  
Verification: Compare the AI summary with the original HR message before sending.

### Usage Frequency
Daily

### Success Criteria
Accurate summaries that require minimal correction.

---

## Task 2: Drafting Engineering Meeting Follow-Ups
### Expected Benefit
Clearer action items and faster communication with engineering teams.

### Preferred Prompt / Workflow
Use an information‑workflow prompt to extract action items from meeting notes.

### Risk / Verification Requirement
Risk: Missing or misinterpreted technical details.  
Verification: Review action items with the meeting notes and confirm with the engineer if needed.

### Usage Frequency
Weekly

### Success Criteria
Action lists that match the meeting discussion and reduce back‑and‑forth clarification.

---

## Task 3: Preparing Restricted Project Access Card Requests
### Expected Benefit
More organized and clearer request drafts for project managers.

### Preferred Prompt / Workflow
Use a planning‑workflow prompt to structure the request without including sensitive project details.

### Risk / Verification Requirement
Risk: Sensitive project information must not be shared with AI.  
Verification: Remove all project identifiers and manually review the final draft before submission.

### Usage Frequency
Weekly

### Success Criteria
Accurate, compliant drafts that are approved quickly by project managers.

---

## Final Statement
This integration plan reflects safe, practical, and responsible AI use in my administrative role. All workflows include human review and avoid sharing sensitive or restricted project information.
